<article class="env-lemma" id="02LH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02LH">Lemma <span data-tag="02LH">37.40.2</span>.</a> Let $f : U \to S$ be a surjective étale morphism of affine schemes. There exists a surjective, finite locally free morphism $\pi : T \to S$ and a finite open covering $T = T_1 \cup \ldots \cup T_ n$ such that each $T_ i \to S$ factors through $U \to S$. Diagram: </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ &  \coprod T_ i \ar[rd] \ar[ld] &  \\  T \ar[rd]^\pi &  &  U \ar[ld]_ f \\  &  S &  }  \]
</div>
  <p> where the south-west arrow is a Zariski-covering. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a restatement of Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00UG" data-tag="00UG">10.144.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>